<section class="ac-blue section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Museum and cultural retail questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Can Teamwork Commerce handle the gift shop, membership and donations on one device?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. The Mobile POS handles gift shop merchandise, membership renewals and donation collection on a single device. It does not sell admission: the ticketing system you already run keeps doing that. Staff can process any transaction type anywhere, in the lobby, gallery, gift shop, or at off-site fundraising events. Donation "round-ups" are built into the core checkout flow, not a plugin.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does this compare to museum-specific POS systems?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Museum-specific systems tend to lead with admissions and treat the shop as an afterthought, which is the opposite of where Teamwork Commerce is strong. We do not sell admission. What we run is the commercial side: enterprise gift shop inventory with RFID, membership and donations in the same transaction, member lifetime value tracked across all of it, mobile POS that travels to an off-site fundraiser, fiscal compliance including Gift Aid, VAT and GST, and SOC 2 Type 2 security for government-funded institutions. It sits alongside your ticketing rather than replacing it.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does this compare to running the shop on a general-purpose POS?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>A general-purpose POS keeps the shop's data in its own world, with no idea who is a member or a donor. Teamwork Commerce puts the gift shop, membership and donations on one record: real-time inventory with RFID, 150+ reports, and mobile POS that works at an off-site event as well as it does in the lobby. Admission stays with the ticketing system you already run.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Can we track member lifetime value across the gift shop, membership and donations?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork's unified CRM creates a single profile for every visitor that aggregates gift shop purchases, membership level and donation history into one "Value to the Institution" metric. This enables targeted fundraising campaigns, personalized staff interactions, and data-driven membership tier strategies.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Does the platform support Gift Aid (UK) and membership-based tax exemptions?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce handles Gift Aid for UK institutions and membership-based tax exemptions natively. The platform is localized in 40+ countries with automated fiscal compliance (VAT, GST, NF525, TSE), making it ideal for international museums and cultural institutions.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Which museums use Teamwork Commerce?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The Broad, MoMA and the Royal Academy of Arts are Teamwork Commerce clients. The platform serves museums and cultural institutions that need the gift shop, membership and donations on one mobile-first platform, with enterprise security (SOC 2 Type 2) and global compliance.</p></div>
      </div>
